Here's a sample CSS code to create the search bar with the described features:
```css
.search-bar {
  width: 100%;
  margin-right: 1em;
  padding: 0.5em;
  border-radius: 5px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  background-color: #f2f2f2;
}

.search-bar input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.5em;
  border: none;
  outline: none;
  background-color: #f2f2f2;
  color: #000;
  font-size: 1rem;
}

.search-bar input::placeholder {
  color: #b6b6b6;
}

.search-bar input:focus {
  border: none;
  outline: none;
  background-color: #fafafa;
}

.search-bar.icon {
  margin-right: 0.5em;
  font-size: 1.2em;
  color: #000;
  transition: color 0.2s;
}

.search-bar.icon:hover {
  color: #0066cc;
}

.search-bar:focus.icon {
  color: #0066cc;
}
```
This will create a search bar with a placeholder text of "Search..." and a magnifying glass icon on the left side of the input field. The icon changes color to blue when the user hovers over it or clicks inside the input field. The border radius and colors of the search bar can be adjusted as needed.

